michapringle@yahoo.com (Micha Pringle) wrote in message news:<6b61d9ec.0401091240.2cd5d080@posting.google.com>...
> What is a good technique for this "midgame", where the character is
> progressing from a 98 pound weakling to a 150 pound Bruce Lee? Is it
> really a good idea to buy as much protection as I can?

If you can afford it, yes, buy protection.  What else are these many
zorkmids of use?  You may dig up all the vaults to get some money if
you don't already have it.

OTOH, you may get protection by physical means which is sufficient to
complete the quest.  Having dragon armor (and few other pieces of armor)
enchanted will quickly boost your AC.  So I'd suggest to find some
appropriate dragon (gray or silver are prefered) deeper in the dungeons.

> Should I just
> go straight to Ludious and Medusa and the Castle after the GM, then
> buy all the AC stuff after (the stuff I couldn't afford on the way
> there that is).

Yes, go to Medusa, but be cautious with the Castle (you should be magic
resistant) and with Ludios (you should have reflection).  If you have
all your stuff for the quest (I value paralysis for this purpose), do
it.  Personally I don't care too much whether I have a couple of HPs and
AC points more or less, but I care well if I know that the quest nemesis
is a magician that will kill me in three turns with his magic.

